{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-reeb-epsilon","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:reeb-epsilon","kind":"definition","title":"The Reeb infinitesimal $\\varepsilon$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-reeb-derivation","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-calculus-up-to-epsilon"],"cites":["references/conway1976","references/gonshor1986"],"tags":["reeb","infinitesimal","derivation","surreal","categorical-primitive","classical-limit"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebEpsilon","text":"reeb-epsilon.md","leanSource":"reeb-epsilon.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:reeb-epsilon\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A)</code> be a quantum observable universe with categorical Reeb derivation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi \\in \\mathrm{Der}(A)</code> (<a href=\"#def:categorical-reeb-derivation\" data-at=\"quantum-observable-universes/algebraic-substrate-reeb\">categorical Reeb derivation</a>), and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi_t : A \\to A</code> denote the one-parameter Reeb flow generated by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi</code>.</p>\n<p>The <strong>Reeb infinitesimal</strong> is the distinguished element</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">\\varepsilon := \\left. \\frac{d}{dt} \\right|_{t = 0} \\Phi_t \\;\\in\\; \\mathrm{Der}(A)</code></pre>\n<p>of the derivation algebra of the substrate object <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/reeb-epsilon.md","heading":"Definition","number":"21.4.16","page":"b/def-reeb-epsilon","qa":{"counts":{"pass":82,"fail":1,"warn":1,"na":10,"